# Code owners for powershell-lsp.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES TODAY: nothing. It is a statement of review ownership in the
# place tooling looks for one. GitHub consults a CODEOWNERS file only when a branch
# protection rule (or ruleset) turns on "Require review from Code Owners". As of
# 2026-08-12 the protection rule on `main` has require_code_owner_reviews = false, so
# this file is inert content and changes no merge behaviour.
#
# HOW IT WOULD BE ACTIVATED (deliberately NOT done):
#   Settings -> Branches -> Branch protection rules -> `main`
#     -> Require a pull request before merging
#       -> tick "Require review from Code Owners"
#
# WHY IT IS NOT ACTIVATED YET -- this is the honest part, not an oversight:
# a code-owner requirement is satisfied only by an approving review FROM a code owner.
# GitHub does not let anyone approve their own pull request; `manderse21` is the sole
# code owner and authors effectively every pull request; and `enforce_admins` is true
# on this repository, so there is no admin bypass. Turning the setting on today would
# make every pull request unmergeable. It becomes enforceable when a second maintainer
# exists -- the open human item in CONTINUITY.md, which no document can close.
#
# See docs/roadmap-ii/GOVERNANCE-SURFACE.md section 4.3 for the full derivation, and
# MAINTAINERS.md for release authority and the second-maintainer on-ramp.

